## Description

The RVV 1.0 specification mandates that a set of instructions raise an illegal-instruction
exception when `vstart != 0` (these instructions cannot be restarted, so `vstart` must be
zero when they begin execution):

| Instruction(s) | Spec reference (`v-spec.adoc`, RVV 1.0) |
|---|---|
| Vector reductions (`vredsum` etc., `vwredsum*`) | L3907 |
| `vcpop.m` | L4196 |
| `vfirst.m` | L4218 |
| `vmsbf.m` | L4259 |
| `vmsif.m` | L4295 |
| `vmsof.m` | L4332 |
| `viota.m` | L4383 |
| `vcompress.vm` | L4797 |

(e.g. L4797: *"The vcompress instruction ... is always executed as if vstart=0; a non-zero
vstart causes an illegal instruction trap"* — analogous wording at the other references.)

On Ara (main), these instructions retire normally with `vstart != 0` — the dispatcher
contains no `vstart`-dependent illegal check for them (grep of `ara_dispatcher.sv` for the
mandatory list finds nothing). Reference simulators (spike with `--isa=rv64gcv`) raise the
illegal-instruction exception for all of them.

This was found by differential testing (isla-generated single-instruction cases): 49 cases
across the mandatory list retired on Ara while spike trapped (class
`BUG_vstart_mandatory_list_ara_retires`, majority `vcompress.vm`).

## Minimal reproducer (`vcompress.vm`)

```asm
# vcompress.vm with vstart=1: RVV 1.0 requires an illegal-instruction trap
.option norvc
.section .text.init
.align 4
.globl _start
_start:
    la t0, init_trap
    csrw mtvec, t0
    li t0, 0x6600
    csrs mstatus, t0              # VS|FS Dirty
    la t0, test_trap
    csrw mtvec, t0
    la sp, _stack_top
    li t1, 4
    vsetvli zero, t1, e32, m1     # vl = 4
    vmv.v.i v2, 1
    vmv.v.i v3, 3
    li t0, 1
    csrw vstart, t0               # vstart = 1 != 0
    vcompress.vm v1, v2, v3       # <-- must trap illegal; Ara retires it
    li a0, 0                      # reached => retired without trap
    j _exit

    .align 2
test_trap:
    csrr a0, mcause
    li t0, 2
    beq a0, t0, 1f
    li a0, 8
    j _exit
1:  li a0, 2                      # illegal-instruction observed
    j _exit

    .align 2
init_trap:
    li a0, 32
    j _exit

    .align 2
_exit:
    li t0, 0xD0000000             # Ara CTRL eoc register
    sd a0, 0(t0)
1:  j 1b

.section .stack
.align 4
.space 4096
_stack_top:
```

Build and run (bare-metal ELF linked at 0x80000000):

```sh
riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -march=rv64gcv -mabi=lp64d -nostdlib -static \
  -T ara.ld -o vcompress_vstart.elf vcompress_vstart.S
# note: -c must come before -l (the emu's argv handling permutes otherwise)
./hardware/build/verilator/Vara_tb_verilator -c 2000000 -l ram,vcompress_vstart.elf,elf
```

## Expected behavior

`vcompress.vm` (and every instruction in the table above) raises an illegal-instruction
exception (mcause=2) whenever `vstart != 0`, as spike does.

## Actual behavior

The instruction retires and writes its result; the exit code of the program above is 0
("retired"), not 2 ("trapped"). The same holds for the other instructions in the mandatory
list (49/49 differential cases).

## Suggested fix

In `ara_dispatcher.sv`, for the decode sites of the mandatory list, add e.g.

```systemverilog
if (csr_vstart_q != '0) illegal_insn = 1'b1;
```

(The vector-reduction and mask-unary sites already track `vstart` for restart purposes, so
the check is a one-liner per site.)

## Environment

- Ara commit: `34bd3bc1` (main at time of report)
- Config: `config=2_lanes` (VLEN=2048, NrLanes=2), Verilator emu
  (`hardware/build/verilator/Vara_tb_verilator`)
- Golden reference: spike (riscv-isa-sim) `--isa=rv64gcv_zvl2048b`, traps all 49 cases
